@startuml
participant "Alice\nlanlink-client-reader" as AR
participant "Alice\nlanlink-file-sender" as AS
participant "Server worker\nlanlink-‹id› (Alice)" as SA
participant "Server worker\nlanlink-‹id› (Bob)" as SB
participant "Bob\nlanlink-client-reader" as BR
participant "Bob main\nthread" as BM

note over AR, BM
Start: Alice sent FILE_OFFER and the server forwarded it to Bob
(TransferSession OFFERED, see Figure 7)
end note

alt Bob rejects the offer
  note over BM
  ∕reject ‹id› [reason]
  reject_file: no
  Receiver, no .part
  end note
  BM ->> SB : FILE_REJECT (transfer_id, reason)
  note over SA, SB
  REJECTED,
  session deleted
  end note
  SB ->> AR : FILE_REJECT
  SB ->> BR : FILE_REJECT echo
  BR ->> BM : event
  note over AR
  SendSession
  REJECTED
  (REJECTED_BY_PEER)
  end note
  note over AR, AS : no sender thread was started
else sender cancels during the chunk loop
  note over AS
  iter_chunks raises
  TransferError, e.g.
  SOURCE_CHANGED (file
  modified while sent).
  SendSession FAILED
  end note
  AS ->> SA : FILE_CANCEL\n(transfer_id,\nreason)
  note over SA, SB
  CANCELLED,
  session deleted
  end note
  SA ->> BR : FILE_CANCEL (reason)
  note over BR
  Receiver:
  _fail_and_cleanup
  deletes .part,
  CANCELLED
  (CANCELLED_BY_PEER)
  end note
  BR ->> BM : final snapshot
end

note over AR, BM
The CLI has no cancel command. SendSession.cancel() and Receiver.cancel()
exist but nothing calls them, so FILE_CANCEL is only sent by
SendSession.outgoing() after a local read error.
end note
@enduml
